First, let's find an expression for $F'(x)$ in terms of $f'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}F'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}F(x)&&\gray{\text{Equivalent notation}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[-1f(x)+3h(x)-3]&&\gray{\text{Substitute the expression for }F(x)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[-1f(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}[3h(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}(3)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=-1f'(x)+3h'(x)-0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $F'(x)=-1f'(x)+3h'(x)$.
